{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Do not lie in wait</b> — Do not desire a wicked man to be one who lies in wait for the dwelling of the righteous. Another interpretation: Do not lie in wait — the wicked man against the dwelling of the righteous, to kill him." "<b>They crouch</b> — The place where his flocks crouch there."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:28.876605049Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}